t of co-founders and Founders like  yourself feel the same way what is one  lesson or one thing that you still are  hoping to learn  that's also a really good question and  the list is really long  and this is uh you know being very  transparent I'm still learning how to  balance your kind of home life and also  the work life and I've become so  invested and so passionate about the  business that at times you forget to  focus on family or your friends or you  know making sure that you have enough  space to you know ensure your mental  health is okay and I think that's that's  something I'm continuing to learn but  one of the things that really in  addition to that that motivates me about  this industry is it's constantly  evolving and I really really love the  technology that we're working on because  it's not just about building a truck  it's we're solving issues that have  never been solved ever before right  building  long-term Lithium-ion batteries that can  be 100 recyclable that that really solve  the climate crisis like those are Big  Technical challenges that every day get  me excited to to just even show up  awesome  um and last question for you yeah where  do you see both yourself and your  company five years from now  uh that's a great question  um I hopefully see myself right where I  am and in terms of you know working with  exos  um personally and and professionally I  think I would like to see a lot more  growth in terms of learning about the  future of the industry the future of how  we can continue to make a difference in  the climate problem that we're dealing  with  um and I really think access will be the  leading solution in this industry you  know I think for us we've seen how the  traditional oems are really slow to act  and to change and they're only doing  this because they're being forced to  we're doing it because we're passionate  about it we want to actually solve a  real problem here and we can do it  profitably and so I think there's  